nderstand the scenario. Do you mean a negative check, verifying something that does not match the index pattern is rolled over? I think the existing `IndexTemplateRegistryTests.testAutomaticRollover` covers that: it creates two logs and one traces data stream, and verifies that only the logs ones are rolled over when updating the logs template.","Not exactly a negative check -- my concern is when plugins operate under normal circumstances then there is no need to rollover on installation. I was thinking of having a test case to cover this scenario to make sure that rollover on installation doesn\u0027t break anything for other plugins. Does it make sense?"],"path":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java","id":36258,"created_at":"2024-11-05T09:58:21Z","original_position":48,"side":"RIGHT","position":48,"submitted_on_commit":"0cff8dbc0d3b90873f1cde6b09283ae47b9273ab","diff_hunk":"@@ -550,8 +549,8 @@ private void putComposableTemplate(\n                     @Override\n                     public void onResponse(AcknowledgedResponse response) {\n                         if (response.isAcknowledged()) {\n-                            if (isUpgrade \u0026\u0026 applyRolloverAfterTemplateV2Upgrade()) {\n-                                invokeRollover(state, templateName, indexTemplate, creationCheck);\n+                            if (applyRolloverAfterTemplateV2Update()) {","submitted_line":552},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The removal of the `isUpgrade` parameter from `putComposableTemplate` simplifies the method signature. However, this change implies that rollover logic will now apply to both upgrades and initial installations, which is consistent with the updated Javadoc but should be confirmed as intended behavior.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/IndexTemplateRegistry.java-x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/template/Ind